VI.II.	Prerequisites & Security Setup
To automate the disk SKU conversion without storing credentials, we utilize an Azure Automation Account leveraging a System Assigned Managed Identity.
Critical Architectural Rule: The Automation Account must be deployed in the exact same Subscription as the ASR Recovery Services Vault, and physically located in a DR Region (e.g., West Europe). If not, ASR will not natively see the runbook.
Automation Account
In the Azure Portal search bar, type Automation Accounts and select the service.
Click + Create and fill in the Basics tab:
Subscription: Must match your ASR Recovery Services Vault subscription.
Resource Group: Create a dedicated RG (if not existent in the subscription) e.g. AEaewPprdRrg-ASRAutomation.
Region: West Europe (DR target region).
Automation Account: Name must be AEwPrdAu-ASRAutomation (adapt naming to the region as per SCOR Cloud Naming Convention)
 


Click Next: Advanced.
Under Identity, ensure System assigned is checked (ON). This is mandatory for secure authentication.
 
Click Next: Networking.
Select Public access (required for the runbook to reach the Azure Resource Manager API ).[la il m'a dit it should be private access est ce que c'est possible ca ?]
Select Private access
 
Click Review + Create, then Create.
RBAC / Permissions
The newly created Managed Identity needs the authority to power off VMs and change disk SKUs specifically within the DR target environment.
Navigate to your Target DR Resource Group (the resource group where the ASR failover VMs and passive replica disks reside). [là il a dit We should provide this right on the whole subscription, not RG by RG possible ca ?]
